Rebuilds the ground roster on Sean's 21 September design. Crown Regulars,
the Reef Guard and the Confederacy's Ship's Company are cut; the Fensworn,
the Hushed, the Brethren, the Bog Witches and the Shoal Wardens replace
them. Both sides now run two companies from the first day and four behind
research at R2, R4, R6 and R8.

The shape it buys: the Crown MAKES its soldiers as the war goes on and the
Confederacy RECRUITS peoples who join it, so research reads as a foundry on
one side and an alliance on the other. The Bog-folk now fight under both
flags — the Fensworn clans for the Crown, the conjure-women against it —
which puts the split-family lore of the Fenrunner and the Witchlight into
the infantry.

Four new numbers per troop: bombardDefense, costGold, days and upkeep. Gold
and days track offense+defense+watch; upkeep is the 1%-of-cost benchmark,
above rate for the made and grown units. The Shoal Wardens are deliberately
under-priced at 16 gold and eight days because their job is meeting the
garrison ladder, not winning fights — blanketing ten sour islands costs 640
gold in Shoal-folk against 1,680 in Crown Marines.

bombardDefense is a separate, much smaller scale from defense on purpose: a
bombarding fleet rolls 1d32 where six troops invading roll 1d180, so one
number cannot serve both dice.

localOf now skips research troops. Without it the Bog Witches and the Shoal
Wardens would stand in starting garrisons on their home islands years
before they join the war.

docs/siege-and-ground-war.md carries the full bombardment and invasion spec
this roster is built for. The resolvers, the deletions and the Defenses
panel are not in this commit.

