From bc45d26b002979fe2529cf70ac1e33e261c6d0b9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 20 Sep 2026 22:24:50 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] Coral comes inside the charts and Windward goes out
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Sean, 21 September: "Let's make the coral reach one of the explored starting
reaches. And the windward one unexplored."

A straight swap of roles rather than a move, because the opening is balanced
on the count — three contested Reaches dealt two islands a side, three
frontier Reaches dark and hiding Freeport — and not on which chains they are.
Tier did not move with role: Windward is still drawn on the inner ring, so
where a chain sits on the map and whether anyone has charted it are two
separate questions now. A dark chain a short sail from the capital is the
better opening anyway, and the Long Sea has forty miles of reef with one
channel through it to explain itself with.

What it nearly broke: Coralhome is handed to the Crown by name, a hundred
lines after the contested Reaches are dealt at random. That was safe only
while its Reach had no deal. Inside the charts, the shuffle could deal the
founding wound to the Confederacy and have the Crown take it back later,
leaving it flying Crown colours while still standing in `allianceSystems` —
where the opening posts Confederate crew and counts Confederate holdings. It
is kept out of the shuffle instead, and there is a test for it.

Four tests were asserting things that were true only because of where the fog
happened to fall, and are fixed to assert the rule instead: charted-ness
follows a Reach's role rather than `isCore`; a Sea summary averages over the
islands you have charted, not every settled one; shipwright craft needs a
slipway, not a slipway or a barracks. And one real bug came out from under the
change — a charting report read "puts The Terraces on the chart", the one
event line of its kind without `inProse` on it.

Measured over twenty-four wars, both sides machine-played, seeds 900-923: the
Crown won ten before and seven after, which is inside the noise for a sample
that size. Nothing compensated.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
